================================================================================
VALIDITY ASSESSMENT OF INFERENCES
================================================================================

1. MODEL CONVERGENCE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Oreobates model converged: True
   Gastrotheca model converged: True

2. PROPORTIONAL ODDS ASSUMPTION
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   The ordinal logistic model assumes proportional odds across categories.
   This means the effect of predictors is constant across different thresholds.
   Violation would suggest using partial proportional odds or multinomial models.
   → Check: Compare AIC/BIC with multinomial logit if concerned

3. SERIAL CORRELATION IN RESIDUALS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Oreobates residual ACF(1): -0.006
   Gastrotheca residual ACF(1): 0.003
   → Lag-1 predictors should capture most autocorrelation
   → ✓ Low residual autocorrelation

4. MULTICOLLINEARITY
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Oreobates design matrix condition number: 43.5
   Gastrotheca design matrix condition number: 43.5
   → Condition number < 30: Good
   → Condition number 30-1000: Moderate multicollinearity
   → Condition number > 1000: Severe multicollinearity

5. SAMPLE SIZE ADEQUACY
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Observations: 2903
   Oreobates parameters: 25 (ratio: 116.1:1)
   Gastrotheca parameters: 25 (ratio: 116.1:1)
   → Rule of thumb: At least 10-20 observations per parameter
   → ✓ Adequate sample size

6. CROSS-SPECIES EFFECTS SIGNIFICANCE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Gastrotheca → Oreobates effect p-value: 0.3372
   → ✗ Not significant
   Oreobates → Gastrotheca effect p-value: 0.4285
   → ✗ Not significant

7. OUT-OF-SAMPLE VALIDATION
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Recommendation: Perform k-fold cross-validation or time-series split
   to assess generalization performance on held-out data.

8. CAUSAL INTERPRETATION CAVEATS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   ⚠ IMPORTANT: These models show ASSOCIATION, not CAUSATION
   • Cross-species 'influence' could reflect:
     - Shared environmental drivers not fully captured
     - Common behavioral responses to unmeasured factors
     - True behavioral interaction
   • Temporal precedence (lags) suggests potential causality but doesn't prove it
   • Experimental manipulation would be needed for causal claims

